{"duration_api_ms":3664,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"4f5cfd92-f37c-41ae-9e7e-3ff74b44dfcf","total_cost_usd":0.0007274,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1023,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":710,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":398},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1023,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":710,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1023,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1023},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1568,"outputTokens":732,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":1023,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0007274,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":398,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":1023,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Spread drivers:** An ETF's quoted spread reflects the market maker's cost to hedge and make a two-sided market. Wide, illiquid, or off-hours underlying baskets raise hedging risk and widen quotes. Hedging costs include executing the basket or a proxy such as futures, plus inventory risk while the hedge is open. Creation and redemption costs set how far the price can drift from NAV before authorized participants arbitrage it back. Fees, taxes, and the cost of delivering or sourcing baskets widen that band and thus the quote.\n\n**Why volume is incomplete:** Historical volume measures secondary-market trading, which can be inflated by a few active participants or short-term flows. It says little about creation/redemption capacity, underlying depth, or stress behavior. Volume may also be fragmented across share classes or listings. Liquidity is better judged by underlying conditions and creation/redemption capacity than by trading activity alone.","ttft_ms":2123,"type":"result","duration_ms":2986,"uuid":"4e68aa9c-fa5c-4f9c-a8af-b38de520e574","ttft_stream_ms":616,"time_to_request_ms":49,"first_content_frame_ms":616,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
